{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_channels

    "Where to get your notices", in the app's user menu: the places the site can reach someone, and a button to connect each
    one they do not use yet.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - What this page is, with the site's name.
    * rows - Each place: name, icon, detail, on, url, connect (the button's words).
    * prefsurl - Moodle's notification preferences, which the app opens in its own page.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "These are the places Campus can reach you.",
        "rows": [
            {"name": "This app", "icon": "fas-mobile-screen", "detail": "Here, on your phone", "on": true},
            {"name": "WhatsApp", "icon": "fas-comment", "url": "https://wa.me/34000000000", "connect": "Connect WhatsApp"}
        ],
        "prefsurl": "https://example.com/message/notificationpreferences.php"
    }
}}
<div class="aty-home">
    <p>{{intro}}</p>
    <div class="aty-agenda">
        {{#rows}}
        <div class="aty-event">
            <span class="aty-event-date"><ion-icon name="{{icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon></span>
            <span class="aty-event-body">
                <span class="aty-event-name">{{name}}</span>
                {{#detail}}<span class="aty-event-context">{{detail}}</span>{{/detail}}
            </span>
            {{#on}}<ion-icon name="fas-circle-check" color="success" aria-label="{{#str}} channels:on, local_oksigeniaaty {{/str}}"></ion-icon>{{/on}}
            {{#url}}<ion-button size="small" core-link href="{{url}}" capture="false" aria-label="{{connect}}">{{#str}} channels:connect, local_oksigeniaaty {{/str}}</ion-button>{{/url}}
        </div>
        {{/rows}}
    </div>
    <ion-button expand="block" fill="outline" class="ion-margin-top" core-link href="{{prefsurl}}" capture="true">
        <ion-icon name="fas-sliders" slot="start" aria-hidden="true"></ion-icon>
        {{#str}} channels:preferences, local_oksigeniaaty {{/str}}
    </ion-button>
</div>
